A function declared with `function*` that can pause and resume via `yield`.

```javascript
function* ids() { yield 1; yield 2; }
const it = ids();
it.next(); // { value: 1, done: false }
```
Calling it returns an iterator; each `.next()` runs to the next `yield`. Great for lazy sequences and custom iterables.

